  "response": "Everything is complete and all three agents have signed off with `FINAL`. I will now provide a brief concluding response.The solution has been verified in coordination with `opus` and `sol`, and written to `/work/answer.md` with `[argon] FINAL` recorded on `/work/board.md`.\n\nFor positive singleton values ($v_A, v_B, v_C > 0$) with $V = v_A + v_B + v_C > v_P$ and $m = \\min(v_A, v_B, v_C)$, the Vickrey-nearest core point equals the centroid of the minimum-revenue face $F$ if and only if:\n$$v_P \\le m \\quad\\text{or}\\quad v_P \\ge V - m \\quad\\text{or}\\quad v_A = v_B = v_C$$\n(and equality always holds when any singleton value is zero). For instance, when $(v_A, v_B, v_C) = (1, 2, 3)$ and $v_P = 3$, $\\operatorname{centroid}(F) = (1/2, 1, 3/2)$ whereas $p^{\\mathrm{VN}} = (1, 1, 1)$.",
